## Summary

Replaces browser-persisted hour-long access tokens with a production-oriented browser session model:

- short-lived typed access JWTs (10 minute default, hard maximum 15 minutes);
- access JWT stored only in web-client memory, never localStorage/sessionStorage;
- opaque rotating refresh token in an HttpOnly cookie;
- separate double-submit CSRF cookie + `X-CSRF-Token` boundary for refresh/logout;
- durable hashed refresh-session state with family replay containment;
- password-change revocation of all refresh sessions;
- fail-closed production cookie/configuration contract.

## Backend safety invariants

- PostgreSQL stores only SHA-256 hashes of refresh and CSRF secrets.
- Refresh rows are pessimistically locked during rotation.
- Successful refresh creates a successor in the same family and marks the old row `ROTATED`.
- Reuse of a rotated credential outside the grace window revokes the active family as `REUSE_DETECTED`.
- Near-simultaneous refresh inside the grace window is rejected without killing the valid successor.
- Expected 401/403 outcomes do not roll back security revocations; unexpected transaction failures still do.
- Suspended users cannot refresh, and the existing JWT filter still reloads user status on every Bearer request.
- Logout always clears browser cookies, including malformed-CSRF failure paths.
- Password changes update the hash and revoke all active refresh sessions in the same DB transaction.
- Ordinary domain endpoints remain explicit Bearer auth; refresh cookies never become ambient API authentication.

## Web client

- removes `dofast.accessToken` from sessionStorage;
- restores a browser session through `/users/session/refresh` after reload;
- coalesces concurrent 401s into one in-flight refresh per tab;
- retries each original request once with the fresh Bearer;
- clears local auth state on refresh failure/logout;
- after password change, immediately logs the first-party client out rather than waiting for the short JWT to expire.

## Production contract

- production access JWT default: 600000 ms;
- production Spring profile hard-wires refresh cookies `Secure=true`;
- production Compose intentionally has no `AUTH_COOKIE_SECURE` override;
- SameSite defaults to `Strict` and only `Strict`/`Lax` are accepted;
- refresh TTL/reuse grace/retention/cleanup settings are forwarded explicitly;
- same-origin web + `/api` deployment remains the expected topology.

## Validation

Exact branch head `1ba33d2ad988f8026aeb28e6364161c99246c0b4` passed push CI:

- API Maven verify ✅
- Web tests/audit/lint/build ✅
- Production Compose contract ✅
- full containers/runtime smoke ✅

The runtime gate now includes a real browser-session smoke against Docker/PostgreSQL. It verifies login cookie attributes, bad-CSRF rejection, successful rotation, exactly one active successor, hash-only persistence, Bearer access after refresh, cookie clearing and server-side revocation after logout.

## Migration

Adds `V50__auth_refresh_sessions.sql`.

## Merge gate

Do not merge unless all PR-triggered workflows are green for this exact latest head SHA and `master` has not moved underneath the branch. Merge method must be a merge commit.

